.SS "\fBInterfaceMetadata\fP getInterfaceMetadata (string interfaceName = \fRundefined\fP, string memberName = \fRundefined\fP)"

.PP
Return an independent structured description of the available interface\&. With both arguments omitted, returns the module inventory, including classes, constants, functions, inherited methods, overload parameter lists, defaults, return contracts, and shared record and callback schemas\&. With interfaceName, returns that class or root export\&. With both names, returns the selected member and all its overloads\&. Use "pdg" as interfaceName to select a root member\&.

.PP
No constructors, methods, or property getters are invoked\&. Exports unavailable in the current build are omitted\&. Every result is an independent copy; changing it does not change subsequent queries\&. Accessor values are not evaluated\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinterfaceName\fP Optional interface or root export name\&. 
.br
\fImemberName\fP Optional member name within the selected interface\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A plain metadata record\&. Invalid selector types throw TypeError; unknown names throw RangeError\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const move = pdg\&.getInterfaceMetadata('Polygon', 'moveTo');
for (const params of move\&.params) {
    console\&.log(params\&.map(param => param\&.type + ' ' + param\&.name)\&.join(', '));
}
console\&.log(pdg\&.describeInterface('Polygon', 'moveTo'));
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBpdg::describeInterface\fP 
.RE
.PP

